.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "docutils\&.parsers\&.rst\&.directives\&.choice ( argument,  values)"

.PP
.nf
Directive option utility function, supplied to enable options whose
argument must be a member of a finite set of possible values (must be
lower case)\&.  A custom conversion function must be written to use it\&.  For
example::

    from docutils\&.parsers\&.rst import directives

    def yesno(argument):
        return directives\&.choice(argument, ('yes', 'no'))

Raise ``ValueError`` if no argument is found or if the argument's value is
not valid (not an entry in the supplied list)\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS "docutils\&.parsers\&.rst\&.directives\&.class_option ( argument)"

.PP
.nf
Convert the argument into a list of ID-compatible strings and return it\&.
(Directive option conversion function\&.)

Raise ``ValueError`` if no argument is found\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS "docutils\&.parsers\&.rst\&.directives\&.directive ( directive_name,  language_module,  document)"

.PP
.nf
Locate and return a directive function from its language-dependent name\&.
If not found in the current language, check English\&.  Return None if the
named directive cannot be found\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS "docutils\&.parsers\&.rst\&.directives\&.encoding ( argument)"

.PP
.nf
Verifies the encoding argument by lookup\&.
(Directive option conversion function\&.)

Raises ValueError for unknown encodings\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS "docutils\&.parsers\&.rst\&.directives\&.flag ( argument)"

.PP
.nf
Check for a valid flag option (no argument) and return ``None``\&.
(Directive option conversion function\&.)

Raise ``ValueError`` if an argument is found\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS "docutils\&.parsers\&.rst\&.directives\&.format_values ( values)"

.SS "docutils\&.parsers\&.rst\&.directives\&.get_measure ( argument,  units)"

.PP
.nf
Check for a positive argument of one of the units and return a
normalized string of the form '<value><unit>' (without space in
between)\&.
(Directive option conversion function\&.)

To be called from directive option conversion functions\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS "docutils\&.parsers\&.rst\&.directives\&.length_or_percentage_or_unitless ( argument,  default = \fC''\fP)"

.PP
.nf
Return normalized string of a length or percentage unit\&.
(Directive option conversion function\&.)

Add <default> if there is no unit\&. Raise ValueError if the argument is not
a positive measure of one of the valid CSS units (or without unit)\&.

>>> length_or_percentage_or_unitless('3 pt')
'3pt'
>>> length_or_percentage_or_unitless('3%', 'em')
'3%'
>>> length_or_percentage_or_unitless('3')
'3'
>>> length_or_percentage_or_unitless('3', 'px')
'3px'

.fi
.PP
 
